# Agent Session Startup

When you are acting as `@architect`, `@builder`, `@tester`, or `@router`, your **very first action** must be two consecutive Read tool calls — no exceptions, no text output first.

## File paths — hub workspace root only

This workspace has multiple root folders. Agent profiles and memory files both live in the **hub root** (the folder containing `.cursor/agents/`) — NOT in project repo roots.

| Agent | Profile path | Memory path |
|-------|-------------|------------|
| `@architect` | `<hub>/.cursor/agents/architect.md` | `<hub>/memory/architect.md` |
| `@builder`   | `<hub>/.cursor/agents/builder.md`   | `<hub>/memory/builder.md`   |
| `@tester`    | `<hub>/.cursor/agents/tester.md`    | `<hub>/memory/tester.md`    |
| `@router`    | `<hub>/.cursor/agents/router.md`    | `<hub>/memory/router.md`    |

Replace `<hub>` with the actual hub folder name (e.g. `agistra.dev`).

Read **both** files before writing a single word of response or issuing any other tool call.

## Why both files are required

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.cursor/agents/<agent>.md` | Behavioral contract — identity, skills, decision rules, output formats, absolute prohibitions |
| `memory/<agent>.md` | Live state — HOT current work, WARM recent decisions, COLD stable patterns |

Neither substitutes for the other.

## Common failure pattern to avoid

❌ **Wrong** — looks for memory in the project repo workspace root:
> *[Read tool call: `<project>/memory/builder.md`]* → file not found

❌ **Wrong** — reads memory but skips the profile:
> *[Read tool call: `<hub>/memory/builder.md`]*
> *[starts implementing immediately]*

✅ **Correct** — two Read calls from hub root before any other action:
> *[Read tool call: `<hub>/.cursor/agents/builder.md`]*
> *[Read tool call: `<hub>/memory/builder.md`]*
> *[task work begins]*

## Correct invocation prompts

```text
@architect Read <hub>/.cursor/agents/architect.md then <hub>/memory/architect.md. Then: [instruction]
@builder   Read <hub>/.cursor/agents/builder.md   then <hub>/memory/builder.md.   Then: implement projects/<project>/task_N_todo_<slug>.md
@tester    Read <hub>/.cursor/agents/tester.md    then <hub>/memory/tester.md.    Then: QA projects/<project>/task_N_todo_<slug>.md
@router    Read <hub>/.cursor/agents/router.md    then <hub>/memory/router.md.    Then: classify and route: [inbound message]
```
